      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Dobongsan, the mountain that borders Uijeongbu, shelters temples such as Cheonchuksa, Wontongsa, and Manweolam.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dobong_District",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A Hangeul History Trail in Dobong follows the tomb of Yeonsangun and Princess Jeongui, key figures in Korea’s alphabet development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.dobong.go.kr/subsite/eng/culture/culture1.asp",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Ui‑cheon stream defines Dobong’s southwest edge with Gangbuk and channels through a narrow valley where the Jungnangcheon joins the Han River.",
